{
  "assumptions": [
    "The accepted Oldale house is retained unchanged. Other roof depths use the same editable 45-degree projection assumption unless explicitly specified.",
    "Building source crops exclude adjoining trees and signs. Palette roles are authored per building region; palette 2 is the surrounding outdoor ground in these drawings, not a universal green-color filter.",
    "Unseen walls repeat a selected wall patch, and roofs repeat a selected roof patch at one source pixel per voxel. Named emblems and roof fixtures are separate parts.",
    "Tree and shrub depth follows the inspected silhouette with circular horizontal sections. Leaf shading does not set depth. Painted forest shadows and neighbouring canopy fragments are excluded from tree geometry.",
    "Broad trees include the five-pixel pointed crown above the repeating 32-pixel unit. Six adjacent floor variants clear matching fragments; optional experimental foliage adds upright clumps to the two encounter-grass variants.",
    "Where painted shadow obscures the lowest trunk row, repeat the last visible wood cross-section down to the ground at native pixel scale.",
    "The Oldale Mart and adjoining tree share a source metatile. The tree owns that cell; the Mart retains its tile-definition guard so cropping cannot make it match unrelated city variants.",
    "The pack contains static scenery. Characters, field effects, interiors, cave terrain and bespoke landmarks require separate recipes.",
    "Experimental encounter grass uses four clumps with six-to-twelve-pixel blades and separate one-pixel stepped leaf bases. Their connecting roots sit below the floor so source ground can show between tufts. Source palette 2 indices 4, 12 and 15 supply leaves, with green shoulders and sparse pale tips; ground index 13 remains floor-owned. Height is authored separately from the elevated sprite projection; voxels and native texels retain their scale. Flexible geometry follows authored terrain; it is opt-in and visually unapproved. Round shrubs keep their own native edge texels instead of repeating a rectangular side patch."
  ],
